WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.337 --> 00:00:08.258
- Throughout history, meteorites
have captivated human imagination.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.191
Each one of these stones
from darker worlds has its own story.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.529
And the bigger ones
have changed entire landscapes.

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:35.911
But they also have left
a deep impact on cultures.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.293
Our voyage took us to
wherever large fireballs

00:00:43.377 --> 00:00:45.420
have plunged down to Earth.

00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:47.422
- It's a very special place for us.

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:50.551
That's where we feel
the presence of our ancestors.

00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:54.429
- How might the church react
if NASA detects

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:57.266
a really threatening object
hurtling towards us?

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.602
- I'll be honest. We'll pray.
(laughs)

00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:01.895
What else can you do?

00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:04.481
- Every element in our body

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:07.317
was synthesized in other stars
before it got here.

00:01:10.404 --> 00:01:12.531
So, yeah, we're all stardust.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.202
- Meteorites have meaning.

00:01:17.286 --> 00:01:18.620
- Whoa! (laughs)

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.833
- The task of humanity is to interpret
what that meaning is.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:26.628
- When a loved one departs
this life to the next,

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:29.173
that transition is done
through the stars.

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:33.719
- We do not know
what in the future is coming at us.

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:39.099
Untold numbers of these voyagers from afar
are still on their way.

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.561
- In Himalayan mythology,
there's this idea of

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:45.314
cycles of creation
and destruction of the universe.

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:49.026
A meteor impact can wipe out life,

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.819
but also deliver the seeds of life.

